{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-012", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Photovoltaic-thermal heat pump based on bio-based surface coating achieves 77.32% overall efficiency", "content": "<p>Iraqi researchers have developed a PVT heat pump featuring a bio-based TiO₂–linseed-oil coating and three alternative refrigerants. The system achieved up to 77.32% overall efficiency and reduced PV module temperatures by as much as 34 C.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/photovoltaic-thermal-heat-pump-based-on-bio-based-surface-coating-achieves-77-32-overall-efficiency/\">Photovoltaic-thermal heat pump based on bio-based surface coating achieves 77.32% overall ef", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/photovoltaic-thermal-heat-pump-based-on-bio-based-surface-coating-achieves-77-32-overall-efficiency/", "type": "rss"}]}
