{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-014", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Georgia Tech, Bert Thin Films build 24.3%-efficient copper-contacted TOPCon solar cell via LECO", "content": "<p>Georgia Tech-led researchers developed a 24.3%-efficient n-TOPCon solar cell using screen-printed rear copper contacts and LECO, nearly matching a 24.5% silver-contacted reference. The approach sharply reduced contact resistance while limiting copper diffusion, highlighting its potential to lower silver consumption and solar cell manufacturing costs.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/georgia-tech-bert-thin-films-build-24-3-efficient-copper-contacted-topcon-solar-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/14/georgia-tech-bert-thin-films-build-24-3-efficient-copper-contacted-topcon-solar-cell-via-leco/", "type": "rss"}]}
